<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><description>Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</description><link>https://www.france24.com/en/</link><lastBuildDate>Fri, 11 Sep 2026 09:58:41 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category>Reporters</category><title>Nepal: Rescue efforts continue in the aftermath of a flash flooding disaster</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/reporters/20260911-nepal-rescue-efforts-continue-in-the-aftermath-of-a-flash-flooding-disaster</link><description>
Two weeks after the devastating flash floods, the number of dead and missing continues to rise. At Kathmandu’s public hospital, as well as outside the military base in Bidur, hundreds of photographs of missing people have been put up. Hundreds of families come forward, hoping for news – good or bad – of one or more loved ones. A race against time is underway: helping survivors, finding those still alive and identifying the victims. Rescue teams have been carrying out repeated helicopter flights, as air access is now the only way to reach remote areas cut off from the rest of the world. Civil society has also mobilised, particularly Nepal’s Generation Z. From Kathmandu to Betrawati, FRANCE 24's reporters Alban Alvarez and Fantine Dantzer accompanied a humanitarian convoy along one of the country’s most treacherous roads.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9842b8cc-adc2-11f1-b741-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/reporters-11-9-2026.jpeg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9842b8cc-adc2-11f1-b741-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/reporters-11-9-2026.jpeg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">cdd519d4-adc3-11f1-8bfe-bd17830f66bc</guid><pubDate>Fri, 11 Sep 2026 09:41:40 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Alban ALVAREZ</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Israel says destroys Hezbollah tunnels as explosions triggers tremor</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260911-israel-says-destroys-hezbollah-tunnels-as-explosions-triggers-tremor</link><description>
Israel said Thursday it demolished key tunnels built by the Iran-backed Hezbollah group beneath the strategic Ali al-Taher ridge in southern Lebanon, with the force of the explosions enough to trigger a 4.1 magnitude tremor. It comes a few days after Israeli authorities claimed to have taken control of the Ali al-Taher ridge, saying that the pro-Iranian Hezbollah had dug numerous tunnels there, allowing it to attack Israel from this mountainous area.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5dfbd1a8-adc2-11f1-9dc5-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260911-100940-101114-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5dfbd1a8-adc2-11f1-9dc5-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260911-100940-101114-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">630c61ee-adc2-11f1-ba1d-bd17830f66bc</guid><pubDate>Fri, 11 Sep 2026 09:34:01 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>'Clashing narratives': How are young Americans today taught about 9/11?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260911-clashing-narratives-how-are-young-americans-today-taught-about-9-11</link><description>
An estimated 100 million Americans, almost a third of the population, were either not yet born or were too young to remember the September 11 attacks. Now, as the US marks the 25th anniversary of 9/11, how are young people in America being taught about what happened that day and its consequences? France 24's Douglas Herbert takes a look.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/09c52e64-adc1-11f1-a740-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260911-100412-100906-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/09c52e64-adc1-11f1-a740-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260911-100412-100906-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0f31ed2e-adc1-11f1-848e-57429f94a7d1</guid><pubDate>Fri, 11 Sep 2026 09:24:52 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Press Review</category><title>Did the War on Terror succeed? Or did Washington fall into al Qaeda’s trap?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20260911-did-the-war-on-terror-succeed-or-did-washington-fall-into-al-qaeda-s-trap</link><description>
PRESS REVIEW: Friday, September 11– 25 years on from 9/11, the international press reflects on the war on terror, its legacy and its failings. In France, the far-right National Rally party tries desperately to distance itself from the overtly racist comments of one of its security officials, made while on duty for his day job as a police officer. Finally, a fossilised feather may give us new insights into why birds survived the asteroid that killed the dinosaurs.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/dc3bd85c-adb2-11f1-9e7e-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-11266649136aa3ae691c5b85-69544097.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/dc3bd85c-adb2-11f1-9e7e-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-11266649136aa3ae691c5b85-69544097.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">8271fe86-adb3-11f1-ace7-ff2b73643b37</guid><pubDate>Fri, 11 Sep 2026 09:16:34 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Antonia KERRIGAN</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Keeping the memory of 9/11 alive for the younger generation</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260911-keeping-the-memory-of-9-11-alive-for-the-younger-generation</link><description>
On 11 September 2001, millions remember how they saw the World Trade Centre towers being struck by airplanes. But, 25 years after the attacks, how is the memory being passed on to the younger generation who were not around to witness them?
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/78ca73de-adbf-11f1-9592-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260911-100149-100410-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/78ca73de-adbf-11f1-9592-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260911-100149-100410-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">7db50aa8-adbf-11f1-8425-57429f94a7d1</guid><pubDate>Fri, 11 Sep 2026 09:13:37 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Technology</category><title>China, Iran among countries using AI to spy on dissidents and minorities, Anthropic says</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/technology/20260911-anthropic-ai-surveillance-targeting-dissidents-china-iran-west-africa</link><description>
Anthropic said Thursday it had disrupted several state-sponsored surveillance operations using its artificial intelligence models, warning of the growing AI use to target dissidents and minorities. The campaigns, detected between January and July, originated in China, Iran and West Africa and targeted diaspora communities, including Hong Kong pro-democracy activists. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/444bfea2-ad83-11f1-95f4-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/18ca7e8cce34b0b27b7cfbeb5da7fc601d1ac72c.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/444bfea2-ad83-11f1-95f4-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/18ca7e8cce34b0b27b7cfbeb5da7fc601d1ac72c.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">324d3752-ad83-11f1-8bb4-cd4b2b5690d6</guid><pubDate>Fri, 11 Sep 2026 07:35:20 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/444bfea2-ad83-11f1-95f4-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/18ca7e8cce34b0b27b7cfbeb5da7fc601d1ac72c.jpg">© SEBASTIEN BOZON, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Vance calls Democrats 'party of hatred' as he seizes MAGA spotlight</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260911-vance-tries-label-democrats-as-party-of-hatred-seizes-maga-spotlight</link><description>
US Vice President JD Vance launched a virulent attack on the Democratic Party Thursday, accusing them of being the "party of hatred" at day two of the Republican convention ahead of the November midterm elections. With public support for President Donald Trump at record lows, Republican figures are increasingly trying to frame their opponents as dangerous political extremists.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4b830b4a-ada4-11f1-ad78-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26254075475865.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4b830b4a-ada4-11f1-ad78-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26254075475865.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">01f37ddc-ada6-11f1-a8c9-0d85900713cb</guid><pubDate>Fri, 11 Sep 2026 06:45:36 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4b830b4a-ada4-11f1-ad78-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26254075475865.jpg">© Julia Demaree Nikhinson, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Sport</category><title>Lens secure an epic comeback win to kick off their Champions League campaign</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/sport/20260911-lens-secure-epic-comeback-win-kick-off-their-champions-league-campaign</link><description>
Trailing 2-1 to Slavia Prague in the 88th minute, few could have imagined that Lens would go on to win. Yet, in just three minutes, the French side turned the game around, led by their captain Florian Thauvin.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/40f5d62e-ada1-11f1-9f29-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C7Y642Y.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/40f5d62e-ada1-11f1-9f29-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C7Y642Y.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f8f05002-ada0-11f1-8bc8-c5a6054a1ee4</guid><pubDate>Fri, 11 Sep 2026 05:57:52 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/40f5d62e-ada1-11f1-9f29-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C7Y642Y.jpg">© Michal Cizek, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Middle East live: Yemen’s Houthis seize key island in Bab al-Mandab strait</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260911-middle-east-live-trump-says-he-has-no-regrets-about-launching-war-on-iran</link><description>
Yemen's Iran-aligned Houthi rebels took over a key island in the Red Sea, completing their push to seize control of the Bab al-Mandab strait area, a local government official and eyewitnesses said on Friday. Perim Island, also known as Mayyun, sits in the middle of the strategic waterway that links Asia to Europe. Follow our liveblog for the latest updates.
