Russian President Vladimir Putin arrived in New Delhi on Friday for a two-day BRICS summit expected to focus on wars in Ukraine and the Middle East and economic challenges. Putin and Iran’s President Masoud Pezeshkian are due to meet Prime Minister Narendra Modi, while China’s Xi Jinping is also expected to hold talks.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f0d61468-acf3-11f1-ab71-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/7e5fcf827b46397639dc014e8f6942451ecb7847.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f0d61468-acf3-11f1-ab71-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/7e5fcf827b46397639dc014e8f6942451ecb7847.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d205e28a-ad83-11f1-a855-07ef7956a524</guid><pubDate>Fri, 11 Sep 2026 02:08:34 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f0d61468-acf3-11f1-ab71-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/7e5fcf827b46397639dc014e8f6942451ecb7847.jpg">© Sajjad Hussain, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Asia / Pacific</category><title>Hong Kong court sentences Tiananmen vigil activists to between 5 and 7 years in jail</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260911-hong-kong-court-sentences-tiananmen-vigil-activists-to-between-5-and-7-years-in-jail</link><description>
Three activists who had held annual vigils commemorating the Tiananmen Square crackdown were sentenced to between five and seven years in prison Friday for calling for an "end to one-party dictatorship". Prosecutors had argued that China's constitution enshrines the primacy of the Communist Party.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a3a6cd0a-ad92-11f1-b92e-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/a1ca4390fa1cddd8c8e78e0df94a508efc1e3ec4.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a3a6cd0a-ad92-11f1-b92e-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/a1ca4390fa1cddd8c8e78e0df94a508efc1e3ec4.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0042bb60-ad83-11f1-8e0c-07ef7956a524</guid><pubDate>Fri, 11 Sep 2026 01:49:17 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a3a6cd0a-ad92-11f1-b92e-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/a1ca4390fa1cddd8c8e78e0df94a508efc1e3ec4.jpg">© Isaac Lawrence, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Trump absent as New York marks 25 years since 9/11 with first Muslim mayor</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260911-trump-new-york-25-years-9-11-muslim-mayor</link><description>
New York on Friday marks the 25th anniversary of the September 11, 2001 attacks, with President Donald Trump set to attend a ceremony at the Pentagon while Vice President JD Vance and four former presidents join commemorations at Ground Zero, where victims’ relatives will read the names of those killed.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ce2d3c00-a7ff-11f1-9a34-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/c735e013a856f06156c3a257dddd6255f324b2f8.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ce2d3c00-a7ff-11f1-9a34-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/c735e013a856f06156c3a257dddd6255f324b2f8.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f612de0c-ad7f-11f1-a9cf-5ddc1bb97edb</guid><pubDate>Fri, 11 Sep 2026 01:47:42 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ce2d3c00-a7ff-11f1-9a34-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/c735e013a856f06156c3a257dddd6255f324b2f8.jpg">© John Moore, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Yemen's Iran-backed Houthi rebels seize strategic Red Sea port city of Mocha</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260910-yemen-houthis-city-red-sea-iran</link><description>
Yemen’s Houthis seized the strategic Red Sea port city of Mocha on Thursday as their offensive against Saudi-backed government forces intensified. Saudi Arabia launched dozens of airstrikes over the past 24 hours, the Houthis said, after the Iran-backed group carried out attacks on Saudi territory that wounded dozens of people.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6446b3f2-abb0-11f1-b7c5-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/c11f1b5f361174a659ad76cf10d47f1376a66e00.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6446b3f2-abb0-11f1-b7c5-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/c11f1b5f361174a659ad76cf10d47f1376a66e00.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e558ca48-ad68-11f1-8a2a-3522566f6c27</guid><pubDate>Thu, 10 Sep 2026 22:55:18 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6446b3f2-abb0-11f1-b7c5-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/c11f1b5f361174a659ad76cf10d47f1376a66e00.jpg">© AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Sport</category><title>Manchester United thrash Sabah in Champions League return as Fabregas's Como shine in European debut</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/sport/20260910-manchester-united-sabah-champions-league-fabregas-como-european-debut</link><description>
Manchester United marked their Champions League return with a 4-0 rout of Sabah on Thursday, with Matheus Cunha, Bruno Fernandes, Benjamin Sesko and Lisandro Martinez scoring. Bayern Munich thrashed Bodo/Glimt 5-0 as Ballon d'Or nominees Michael Olise struck twice and Harry Kane scored, while Cesc Fabregas's Como impressed on their competition debut.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/07011244-ad5b-11f1-a894-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/554cf9a55acac96b45f8c44b72904788adbe99a5.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/07011244-ad5b-11f1-a894-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/554cf9a55acac96b45f8c44b72904788adbe99a5.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3c8f9068-ad63-11f1-be38-87c4d68b8625</guid><pubDate>Thu, 10 Sep 2026 22:25:34 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/07011244-ad5b-11f1-a894-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/554cf9a55acac96b45f8c44b72904788adbe99a5.jpg">© Darren Staples, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Israel destroys Hezbollah tunnel network in south Lebanon, triggering 4.1-magnitude tremor</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260910-israel-hezbollah-tunnels-lebanon-earthquake</link><description>
Israel said on Thursday it destroyed key tunnels built by Iran-backed Hezbollah beneath the strategic Ali al-Taher ridge in southern Lebanon, completing what it called operational control of the area. Lebanon reported a massive explosion, while the US Geological Survey recorded a magnitude 4.1 tremor nearby.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/33fe30ea-ad7b-11f1-9da7-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AFP-20260910-C7Y769E-v3-MidRes-TopshotLebanonIsraelIranUsWar.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/33fe30ea-ad7b-11f1-9da7-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AFP-20260910-C7Y769E-v3-MidRes-TopshotLebanonIsraelIranUsWar.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">07cce53a-ad61-11f1-97b3-23806945c836</guid><pubDate>Thu, 10 Sep 2026 21:50:24 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/33fe30ea-ad7b-11f1-9da7-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AFP-20260910-C7Y769E-v3-MidRes-TopshotLebanonIsraelIranUsWar.jpg">© AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>A propos</category><title>Space: Europe urged to find its path, from crewed spaceflight to communications</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20260910-space-europe-urged-to-find-its-path-from-crewed-spaceflight-to-communications</link><description>
French President Emmanuel Macron and European Commission President Ursula von der Leyen called on Thursday for Europeans to "act" on a massive scale to find their place against the United States and China in the space race, from communications to crewed spaceflight. Speaking with FRANCE 24's Sharon Gaffney, Svetla Ben-Itzhak, Assistant Professor of Space and International Relations, and Deputy Director of the West Space Scholars Programme at Johns Hopkins University, explains that "Europe does have world-class scientific and industrial capabilities, as well as aspirations, but it lacks the investment, the launch cadence, the scale as well as the degree of political integration that the US and China possess".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/61141a3e-ad5a-11f1-a6a0-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260910-223109-224243-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/61141a3e-ad5a-11f1-a6a0-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260910-223109-224243-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">608d3dd8-ad5b-11f1-b402-23806945c836</guid><pubDate>Thu, 10 Sep 2026 21:05:39 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Sharon GAFFNEY</dc:creator></item><item><category>Eye on Africa</category><title>Ugandan royal succession scandal</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/ugandan-royal-succession-scandal</link><description>
In tonight's edition, a dramatic struggle for control of a throne in Uganda. Also, Rwanda shut down 101 alcoholic beverage factories last month and declared a public health crisis after at least 50 people were killed by contaminated illegal supplies. And Ethiopia celebrates its new year. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/13a0f8d6-ad54-11f1-a4bc-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/WB231224-O-01-20260910-01.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/13a0f8d6-ad54-11f1-a4bc-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/WB231224-O-01-20260910-01.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">cb5b032c-ad54-11f1-8b14-0f702f747911</guid><pubDate>Thu, 10 Sep 2026 20:20:01 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Georja CALVIN-SMITH</dc:creator></item><item><title>🔴 Live: Israel demolition of Hezbollah tunnels in south Lebanon caused 4.1-magnitude quake</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260910-middle-east-live-trump-warns-iran-not-to-get-cute-over-activity-at-pickaxe-mountain</link><description></description><guid isPermaLink="false">a0a8115c-ad53-11f1-aa6e-0f702f747911</guid><pubDate>Thu, 10 Sep 2026 20:12:47 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Business</category><title>Record heat and drought make this year's champagne stronger</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/business/20260910-record-heat-and-drought-make-this-year-s-champagne-stronger</link><description>
For the first time, French champagne producers are allowed to sell their bubbly with more than 13% alcohol, as record heatwaves and drought have resulted in grapes containing unusually high levels of sugar. They fear that climate change may eventually force them to permanently rewrite the rules governing winemaking.  Also in the segment, the European Central Bank raised interest rates for the second time this year amid higher energy costs, as a potential new gas crisis looms over Europe. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bdeb1184-ad52-11f1-bb5c-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-12603946306aa30d269d3261-66292844.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bdeb1184-ad52-11f1-bb5c-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-12603946306aa30d269d3261-66292844.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e8c5856e-ad53-11f1-8464-5f4441d89969</guid><pubDate>Thu, 10 Sep 2026 20:12:35 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Yuka ROYER</dc:creator></item><item><category>Truth or Fake</category><title>Meta tests out putting fact-checking in users’ hands across Latin America</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/meta-tests-out-putting-fact-checking-in-users-hands-across-latin-america-1</link><description>
Meta is expanding its shift away from professional fact-checking. The tech giant announced it's trialling it's crowdsourced "Community Notes" system across 16 countries in Latin America. Meta says the system will only fully roll out once it is confident it works, but critics warn that with misinformation, manipulated images and AI-generated content spreading rapidly, crowdsourced checks may come too late to prevent false claims from reaching millions. Vedika Bahl explains the risks.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bc86acb0-ad50-11f1-baa9-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-12835300406aa309c93f4154-74074622.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bc86acb0-ad50-11f1-baa9-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-12835300406aa309c93f4154-74074622.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1d5c19aa-ad4f-11f1-8947-39b0630bb3ec</guid><pubDate>Thu, 10 Sep 2026 20:11:31 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Vedika BAHL</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>French firefighters on six-week strike after record summer blazes</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/french-firefighters-on-six-week-strike-after-record-summer-blazes</link><description>
Firefighters in France are on strike over a lack of funding for essential emergency services. Their dedication was pushed to the limit in the recent wild fire episodes south of Paris and near Bordeaux. Short comings in the current system were highlighted by these extreme cases. FRANCE 24's Mark Owen speaks with Yael Lecras, Vice-President of the National Union of Professional Firefighters.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/124ce6f8-ad4e-11f1-9307-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260910-211032-211733-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/124ce6f8-ad4e-11f1-9307-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260910-211032-211733-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">48e07360-ad4e-11f1-9b94-03c44d95fcfa</guid><pubDate>Thu, 10 Sep 2026 19:41:24 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>As New York marks 25 years since 9/11, Muslims recall stigmatisation in aftermath of attacks</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/as-new-york-marks-25-years-since-9-11-muslims-recall-stigmatization-in-aftermath-of-attacks</link><description>
As New York marks 25 years since the terrorist attacks on September 11th, New York’s Muslim community has become increasingly part of the fabric of the city. One sign of that is the election of Zohran Mamdani as the city’s mayor last November. Another is the state's largest mosque, due to open its doors at the end of the year. But while things have improved, many Muslims still remember the difficult months that followed the attack. FRANCE 24's Monte Francis reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/05bcffd2-11c1-11ec-9063-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000_9MG36Z.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/05bcffd2-11c1-11ec-9063-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000_9MG36Z.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ace33aca-ad4c-11f1-9f80-39b0630bb3ec</guid><pubDate>Thu, 10 Sep 2026 19:32:33 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>'No facts': Morocco denies involvement in deadly Ceuta migrant rush</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260910-no-facts-morocco-denies-involvement-in-deadly-ceuta-migrant-rush</link><description>
Moroccan authorities said on Thursday there were "no facts" establishing its involvement in the migrant rush into Spain's North African exclave of Ceuta in July. It was the kingdom's first official response to a Spanish police report accusing its security forces of "total permissiveness" when the mass crossing took place.
